@node Main "WHDSelector"

                         @{b}WHDSelector@{ub}
                    by HiFi - enjoy the usage!

  WHDSelector browses, downloads, installs and plays software from four
  sources, all in one MUI window:

    - Retroplay WHDLoad packs (games, demos, magazines)
    - Aminet
    - Modland music modules (Amiga formats)
    - Scene.org party releases (Amiga compos)

  @{" Requirements          " link Requirements}
  @{" Installation          " link Install}
  @{" The main window       " link Window}
  @{" Retroplay WHDLoad     " link Retroplay}
  @{" Aminet                " link Aminet}
  @{" Modland music         " link Modland}
  @{" Scene.org parties     " link Scene}
  @{" Playing music         " link Playing}
  @{" Settings              " link Settings}
  @{" History and log       " link History}
  @{" Menus                 " link Menus}
  @{" Files                 " link Files}
  @{" Credits               " link Credits}
@endnode

@node Requirements "Requirements"
@{b}Requirements@{ub}

  - AmigaOS 3.1 or newer, 68000 or better (68020+ recommended)
  - MUI 3.8 or newer and NList.mcc
  - A TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (Miami, Roadshow, AmiTCP)
  - C:lha (and C:unlzx for .lzx, unzip for .zip archives)
  - HippoPlayer for playing music (optional)

  Downloads use plain HTTP; no SSL library is needed.
@endnode

@node Install "Installation"
@{b}Installation@{ub}

  Copy WHDSelector and WHDSelector.guide into one drawer, for example
  Work:WHDSelector. Everything WHDSelector writes stays in that drawer
  unless you choose other directories in @{"Settings" link Settings}:

    temp/          downloaded lists (WHDLoad DATs, Aminet, Modland)
    GameFiles/     WHDLoad archives and installs (default)
    Aminet/        Aminet packages (default)
    Music/         Modland modules (default)

  Start WHDSelector from Workbench or Shell. Put your TCP/IP stack
  online first; if it is offline, WHDSelector still opens and you can
  browse lists already downloaded. It connects when you press
  @{b}Refresh list@{ub} or @{b}Download selected@{ub}.
@endnode

@node Window "The main window"
@{b}The main window@{ub}

  @{b}Source@{ub}     Retroplay WHDLoad, Aminet or Modland (music).
  @{b}Pack / Category / Format@{ub}
             What part of the source is listed.
  @{b}Letter@{ub}     Shows only names starting with a letter (Modland: the
             author's initial).
  @{b}Search@{ub}     Filters the list while you type (Modland "All
             formats": type and press Return to search everything).

  @{b}Browse@{ub} tab   the list. Select several rows with Shift or Ctrl and
               a click.
  @{b}History@{ub} tab  what was downloaded and when, newest first.

  @{b}Download selected@{ub}  downloads and installs the selected rows.
  @{b}Play@{ub}               plays the selected Modland module.
  @{b}Stop@{ub}               stops after the title being downloaded.
  @{b}Refresh list@{ub}       fetches the newest list for the current source.
  @{b}Settings...@{ub}        directories, filters and HippoPlayer.

  The status line and the log at the bottom tell what is going on.
@endnode

@node Retroplay "Retroplay WHDLoad"
@{b}Retroplay WHDLoad@{ub}

  Packs: Games, Games (Beta & Unofficial), Demos, Demos (Beta &
  Unofficial) and Magazines. Columns: title, version, information
  (AGA, NTSC, language...) and size.

  Downloading and extracting is done by the built-in whdfetch engine, so
  archives and drawers are exactly as whdfetch makes them. Titles that are
  already downloaded or extracted are skipped.

  Note: the server allows 500 files (100 GiB) per 7 days over HTTP.
@endnode

@node Aminet "Aminet"
@{b}Aminet@{ub}

  The first category, @{b}Recent (last 14 days)@{ub}, shows the newest
  uploads. The other categories are Aminet's top-level directories.
  Columns: name, category, size, age and description. Search also matches
  descriptions.

  Archives (.lha, .lzh, .lzx, .zip) are extracted into a drawer of their
  own: <Aminet directory>/<name>/. Other files (DMS and ADF disk images,
  pictures, music, documents) are saved there as they are.
@endnode

@node Modland "Modland music"
@{b}Modland music@{ub}

  Modland holds almost 100,000 modules in formats that play on an Amiga:
  Protracker, Soundtracker, Startrekker, OctaMED, AHX, HivelyTracker,
  Future Composer, TFMX, DigiBooster, Musicline, Oktalyzer, Art Of Noise,
  BP SoundMon, Sonic Arranger, SidMon, Delta Music, Digital Mugician,
  JamCracker, Symphonie and DeliTracker Custom.

  @{b}All formats@{ub} (first Format entry) lists every format by the
  author's initial. Type a song or an author into Search and press
  Return to search all formats, for example "space debris".

  Modules are saved as <Music directory>/<author>/<module>. Spaces become
  "_" and names are shortened to 30 characters for the FFS file system.

  Some formats use two files (for example TFMX mdat.* and smpl.*); select
  both.
@endnode

@node Scene "Scene.org parties"
@{b}Scene.org parties@{ub}

  Party releases from the scene.org archive (ftp.scene.org, plain HTTP).
  Choose a Year@{ub} and press Refresh list@{ub}: WHDSelector reads
  every party of that year and lists the files of all compos with
  "amiga" in their name (demo, intro, graphics, music...). This reads many
  pages and takes a while, but only once per year.

  Columns: name, party, compo and size. Downloads go to
  <Demos directory>/<party>/<name>/; archives are extracted, disk images
  and pictures are saved as they are.
@endnode

@node Playing "Playing music"
@{b}Playing music@{ub}

  Select a Modland module and press @{b}Play@{ub}, or double-click it.
  WHDSelector downloads it if needed and plays it in HippoPlayer through
  HippoPlayer's ARexx port. If HippoPlayer is not running, it is started
  from the path given in @{"Settings" link Settings}.

  Whether a format plays depends on HippoPlayer and the player libraries
  you have installed (for example OctaMED modules may need medplayer
  libraries).
@endnode

@node Settings "Settings"
@{b}Settings@{ub}

  @{b}Install directory@{ub}   where WHDLoad titles are extracted.
  @{b}Delete archives@{ub}     remove the archive after extracting.
  @{b}Aminet directory@{ub}    where Aminet packages go.
  @{b}Music directory@{ub}     where Modland modules go.
  @{b}Demos directory@{ub}     where scene.org entries go.
  @{b}HippoPlayer@{ub}         the HippoPlayer program, used to start it.
  @{b}WHDLoad filters@{ub}     hide AGA, CD32/CDTV, NTSC or non-English
                      titles (used on the next Refresh list).

  Settings are saved in whdfetch.ini next to the program, so the
  whdfetch command line tool uses the same directories.

  @{b}MUI settings...@{ub} in the Project menu changes fonts, colours and
  the look of WHDSelector's window.
@endnode

@node History "History and log"
@{b}History and log@{ub}

  The @{b}History@{ub} tab lists every downloaded title with date, time,
  source and target directory. It is stored in WHDSelector.history;
  @{b}Clear history@{ub} empties it (the files themselves stay).

  The log at the bottom of the window shows what WHDSelector does,
  including the messages of whdfetch and the extractors. It is also
  written to WHDSelector.log.
@endnode

@node Menus "Menus"
@{b}Menus@{ub}

  @{b}Project@{ub}
    About...          version and credits
    About MUI...      MUI information
    Manual...         this guide
    Settings...       the settings window
    MUI settings...   MUI preferences for WHDSelector
    Quit

  @{b}Edit@{ub}
    Copy              copies the names of the selected rows
    Paste             pastes clipboard text into Search
    Select all        selects every row of the list
@endnode

@node Files "Files"
@{b}Files@{ub}

  WHDSelector              the program
  WHDSelector.guide        this manual
  whdfetch.ini             settings (shared with whdfetch)
  WHDSelector.log          activity log (kept below 256 KB)
  WHDSelector.history      download history
  temp/                    downloaded lists and indexes
@endnode

